From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spacemit-k3: clear EXTRAVERSION so the kernel packages

The edge tree (AFOliveira/linux riscv/k3-v7.2.6-arch2) ships
EXTRAVERSION = -arch2, so the kernel installs itself as
vmlinuz-7.2.6-arch2-edge-spacemit-k3.

Armbian does not see that suffix: grab_version() in
lib/functions/compilation/utils-compilation.sh keeps EXTRAVERSION only when it
matches ^-rc[0-9]+, so it computes 7.2.6 and packaging then looks for
vmlinu*-7.2.6-edge-spacemit-k3. Nothing matches, nullglob drops the pattern,
the bare `ls` lists the kernel source tree instead, and the build dies in
basename with "extra operand 'Documentation'" after a full successful compile.

Clear EXTRAVERSION. The kernel then reports 7.2.6-edge-spacemit-k3, the same
shape every other Armbian kernel uses, and the upstream revision stays recorded
in the artifact version (the S<sha> field) where Armbian actually reads it.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -5,2 +5,2 @@ SUBLEVEL = 6
-EXTRAVERSION = -arch2
+EXTRAVERSION =
 NAME = Baby Opossum Posse
